From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:20:37 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-s32x

Sega 32X gets one shelf, Games/32X, on PicoDrive (picodrive) alone.
Platform::S32x is appended to SHELVES and Core::Picodrive to EVERY;
upstream's ALL lists stay as they are. Carts are .32x and .bin. A .32x
always lists; a .bin lists only with a 32X header, "SEGA 32X" at 0x100 or
"MARS CHECK MODE" at 0x3c0 (slot_store::s32x), because .bin is also a
Mega Drive extension, and a .bin without either is logged and left off.
The Mega Drive shelf is not touched: it still lists every .md, .gen and
.bin, a 32X game left there included, on Genesis Plus GX. The title comes
from the Mega Drive header, as for Mega Drive.

Every policy method answers 32X explicitly and the same as Mega Drive:
the six-button pad through X, Y, L1 and R1, Select+X flips the picture,
no core picker, no crop, Stretch by default following the frame width, a
4:3 choice, rewind on, the 320x224 picture on the 360x240 canvas. Its
shader is stored in Config/s32x_shader.txt and offers the retro list.
Saves/32X, States/32X and Labels/32X are made at boot. The shelf shows
the Mega Drive cart until the 32X cart lands.
